(in-ns 'go.arbace.py) ^{:go/comments [[3 1 "// Functions, built-in functions, cells, code objects and modules."] [13 1 "// Function is a Python function: a code object with its globals, defaults and closure"] [14 1 "// (CPython's PyFunctionObject)."] [21 20 "// positional defaults, or nil"] [22 20 "// keyword-only defaults, or nil"] [24 20 "// __annotate__, or nil"] [25 20 "// __type_params__, or nil"] [26 20 "// __dict__, made on first use"] [29 2 "// GlobalsMap is the globals when FunctionType(code, globals) was given a dict subclass's instance (queue 205f:"] [30 2 "// annotationlib's _StringifierDict), Globals its dict: the function's global loads go through its __getitem__"] [31 2 "// (CPython's LOAD_GLOBAL on non-exact globals, PyMapping_GetOptionalItem: its __missing__), nil for a dict"] [37 1 "// Builtin is a function implemented in Go (CPython's builtin_function_or_method)."] [41 14 "// the bound object of a method, or nil"] [42 2 "// objectDescr: object's method that left object's dict through the class (methodDescrs[b] is ObjectType)"] [44 2 "// wakeup: a task's task_wakeup, a node of finalize.go's graph (a pending task's cycle runs through it)"] [50 1 "// Cell is a closure's cell; Value nil is empty (unbound)."] [55 1 "// CodeObject is a code object as a Python value (the IR's {:code ...} constants)."] [60 1 "// Module is a module: its name and namespace."] [64 2 "// Cls is a subclass of module this module is an instance of (six's _LazyModule, queue 205), nil for module itself"] [75 1 "// builtinFuncModules are the built-in modules' functions' modules (PY6d's REQUEST: a function's __module__,"] [76 1 "// CPython's m_module, which pickle saves it by)."] [93 37 "// one allocation (queue 210: append grew it a second time)"] [98 4 "// method_check_args (PY7: dict.update() was a Go panic, test_ordered_dict's"] [99 4 "// CPythonBuiltinDictTests.test_update)"] [109 2 "// builtin_function_or_method's __module__ (PY6d's REQUEST): a module's function's module, a builtin's"] [110 2 "// \"builtins\", else None (pickle's whichmodule then finds the function in sys.modules)"] [126 2 "// methodobject.c's meth_reduce (PY6d's REQUEST: pickle saves a built-in function by name): a function's"] [127 2 "// qualified name, a bound method as getattr(self, name)"] [139 3 "// CPython's \"at 0x...\", the address an identity number (asyncio's Handle reprs and their tests: PY6h's"] [140 3 "// REQUEST, queue 200)"] [149 2 "// cell([contents]): Objects/cellobject.c's cell_new, cell_repr and cell_richcompare (queue 205f: annotationlib's"] [150 2 "// _build_closure makes the stringifiers' cells)"] [171 35 "// tp_richcompare without tp_hash: hash() refuses a cell"] [181 3 "// empty cells come before anything else (cell_compare_impl)"] [207 3 "// module_repr: importlib's _module_repr once importlib is the import system (PY6b's request)"] [213 4 "// importlib's _module_repr: a module with a location is \"from\" it"] [218 2 "// module(name, doc=None), CPython's module_init; a subclass's instance (queue 205: six's _MovedItems) made empty"] [219 2 "// as new_module makes it, its __init__ (module.__init__ through super()) filling it"] [257 15 "// module itself: New initialized it"] [261 2 "// module_getsets: __annotations__ and __annotate__ (PEP 649), data descriptors before the dict"] [266 38 "// a subclass's instance: its class's data descriptors first"] [290 4 "// a subclass's instance: the generic lookup (its class's descriptors around the dict), then the"] [291 4 "// dict's __getattr__ (module_getattro)"] [303 23 "// PY6a (enum's global_enum): module_getattro's data descriptors first"] [314 3 "// the type's methods (__dir__, __repr__ ...), then the module's __getattr__ (PEP 562)"] [323 2 "// module.__dir__ (module_dir, queue 223: traceback's suggestions call it): the dict's __dir__ function called,"] [324 2 "// else the dict's keys"] [344 1 "// functionNew is function(code, globals, name=None, argdefs=None, closure=None, kwdefaults=None), types.FunctionType"] [345 1 "// called: Objects/funcobject.c's func_new (its clinic's argument checks, then func_new_impl's in its order, and their"] [346 1 "// messages) over PyFunction_New (the code's name, qualname and docstring, the globals' __name__ as __module__, the"] [347 1 "// builtins from the globals' __builtins__). Queue 205f: annotationlib's FORWARDREF and STRING formats call an"] [348 1 "// __annotate__'s code with a _StringifierDict as its globals (typing.NamedTuple's annotated classes, pip's import)."] [414 2 "// _PyEval_BuiltinsFromGlobals: the globals' __builtins__ (a module its dict), else the running frame's"]] :go/pos {:name [1 9] :package [1 1]} :go/semis [[81 58] [82 39] [100 27] [113 31] [116 36] [120 58] [133 34] [152 38] [155 41] [208 42] [212 47] [250 41] [256 26] [296 41] [311 39] [315 43] [318 40] [337 30] [362 12] [362 19] [371 31] [377 34] [383 34] [391 37] [404 29] [407 12] [407 19] [415 40] [416 26] [418 31] [423 26]]} (go/file "func.go" :imports [])

